 "notes": [
  "The machine is shared with other benchmark runs; the minimum describes the operation, the median shows how contended that run was.",
  "Contiguous-lengths descriptors take the fused Metal kernel; non-contiguous input, non-exact prefixes/suffixes and small shapes take the aten composition.",
  "scan_bounds builds the boundary table and validates it on device; strict validation uses one deferred host read overlapped with the reduction kernel.",
  "per_row_1024x4096 runs one SIMD group per segment along the axis; wide cases assign lanes to inner columns in whole SIMD groups up to 512.",
  "backward is bounds-driven with edge filling, avoiding the position map entirely.",
  "fp32 sum/mean/prod accumulate in a different order on the two devices; max/min are bit-exact.",
  "fp16/bf16 sums accumulate in float32 in the fused kernel then narrow once, matching the CPU kernel within tolerance.",
  "unsafe=True skips only the lengths-sum check; the negative-length and unsorted-offset checks and their one host read still run.",
  "index_reduce_ on MPS is reached only on the aten fallback path.",
  "stages.* are per-launch GPU costs amortizing one synchronization over 60 submissions, so they exclude the round trip the fused call pays once."
